# Documentation layout

- Do not create planning, release, agent-brief, or checklist markdown at the
  repository root. Put it under `docs/` using
  `docs/README.md` (directory map).
- Only these four trackers live directly under `docs/`:
  `SSCRE_PLAN.md`, `SSCRE_PROJECT_ANALYSIS.md`,
  `SSCRE_LEARNING_AND_EXECUTION_GUIDE.md`, `SSCRE_SYSTEM_DESIGN.md`.
- Use `docs/internal/` for release prep and private briefs, `docs/reference/`
  for technical specs, `docs/setup/` for environment setup, `docs/phase-1/`,
  `docs/phase-2/`, `docs/phase-3/`, and `docs/phase-4/` for milestone and
  workstream material.
- Keep new Phase 2–4 filenames in `docs/phase-2/`, `docs/phase-3/`, and
  `docs/phase-4/` (flat folders). Code and benchmarks reference those paths;
  do not nest phase files without updating every reference.
- When adding a notable file under `docs/phase-1/`, `docs/phase-2/`,
  `docs/phase-3/`, `docs/phase-4/`, or `docs/internal/`, add a row to that
  folder's `README.md` index and update `docs/README.md` if the directory map
  or phase table is stale.
- When closing a Phase 3 workstream plan step or promoting feature cards, update
  in the same pass: [`docs/phase-3/PHASE_3_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`](../docs/phase-3/PHASE_3_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md)
  (Status, relevant workstream section, baseline gaps), linked evidence paths,
  and [`docs/phase-3/README.md`](../docs/phase-3/README.md) if new files were
  added. Do not leave the parent plan describing pre-close gaps.
- Markdown links from flat `docs/phase-2/`, `docs/phase-3/`, or `docs/phase-4/`
  files to repository-root paths (`src/`, `tests/`, `benchmarks/`, `artifacts/`,
  `experiments/`) must use the `../../` prefix (e.g.
  `../../src/sscre/cache.py`), not `../src/...`.
- Phase 3 `*EVIDENCE.md` headers must match the cited frozen JSON artifact
  (`git_commit`, `config_sha256`, and split proof: `split_manifest_sha256` on
  held-out runs or `development_sha256` on development-only runs). If prose
  predates a rerun, state that the artifact JSON header is authoritative.
- When [`PHASE_3_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`](../docs/phase-3/PHASE_3_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md)
  definition-of-done is satisfied, its top **Status** must not remain
  `partially complete` without naming the explicit remaining scope (e.g.
  `SSCRE_PLAN.md` §20 int8 row left unchecked by design).
- When moving or renaming docs, search the repo for the old path and update
  links in markdown, Python docstrings, and JSON metadata.
